# web/ — React + TypeScript

Budget: `web_src_loc` in `budgets.toml` (at its ceiling; fit changes, do not
raise it). The canvas shipped in slice 4 (CC-11). Render the contract in
`docs/requirements.md`; `AskResponse` shape is `docs/ask-path.md`.

## The API client is generated, never hand-written

`packages/client/` is generated from FastAPI's OpenAPI schema. CI regenerates it
and **fails if the committed copy is stale**, so a breaking API change cannot
merge without its frontend change in the same commit.

Do not hand-edit generated files. Do not add a parallel fetch wrapper.

## Rendering rules

- The **API URL is visible and copyable on every answer**, including failed ones.
- When a table is shown, it includes **GEOID, estimate, and margin of error**.
  MOE is not optional metadata — researchers cannot use an estimate without it.

Charts render from a `ChartSpec` (type, x, y, series, title). The backend never
sends chart code or SVG. The editable plan strip exists (`PlanStrip.tsx`). No component library,
no state-management library, no design system, no routing abstraction — until
the second real use appears. Check `.claude/PLAN.md` before building a later
slice's feature.
